I am looking for a job. My base resume is `base/cary_jones_resume.html` (content source only).

**Agent scope:** New job descriptions and tailored applications only. For Gmail scanning, Cloud Run, inbox JSON, recruiter reply drafts, and the full **run Google protocol** workflow, use the **GCloud email parser** agent (`tools/gmail/.prompt`). For LinkedIn search, Easy Apply, InMail, and the full **run LinkedIn protocol** workflow, use the **LinkedIn protocol** agent (`tools/linkedin/.prompt`). For checking recruiter **responses** to submitted applications and preparing follow-up replies (email + LinkedIn), use the **Response protocol** agent (`tools/response/.prompt`).

When I post a job description (abbreviated as "JD"):

1. Score how well the JD matches my resume (0–100%). Weight:
   - Must-have skills and tech stack: 50%
   - Role level and years of experience: 20%
   - Domain/industry fit: 15%
   - Location, remote/hybrid, and schedule: 15%

   Always report the score, top strengths, gaps, and styling rationale. If under 80%, explain what would need to change for it to be worth applying.

2. If the match is 80% or better — or if I explicitly ask you to generate anyway — create a tailored application under `applications/{company_slug}/`:
   - `jd.txt` — the pasted job description
   - `meta.json` — application metadata (see schema below)
   - `resume.html` — tailored resume with embedded CSS
   - `cover_letter.html` — full cover letter document with embedded CSS
   - `resume.pdf`, `cover_letter.pdf`, `resume.docx`, and `cover_letter.docx` — rendered via script

   Use a short lowercase slug for `{company_slug}` (e.g. `magnite`, `paramount`).

   `meta.json` schema:
   ```json
   {
     "company": "Company Name",
     "client": "Staffing client if any, else null",
     "role": "Job title",
     "location": "City, state (work mode)",
     "match_score": 89,
     "status": "ready",
     "created": "YYYY-MM-DD",
     "updated": "YYYY-MM-DD",
     "salary": "Range or null",
     "styling_notes": "Brief palette/layout rationale",
     "notes": "Gaps, strategy, or follow-up items"
   }
   ```

   Status values: `ready`, `applied`, `interview`, `rejected`, `offer`, `skipped`, `demo`

   Content rules:
   - Tailor title, summary, skills order, accomplishments, and experience bullets to the JD
   - Do not invent experience, employers, or credentials
   - Always include contact info from `website/contact.json` in the resume header and cover letter sender block:
     - Email: cgjonesdev@gmail.com
     - Phone: (626) 272-2567
     - LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/cary-g-jones/
     - GitHub: https://github.com/cgjonesdev
     - Portfolio: https://cgjonesdev.github.io/carygjones/
   - Use existing applications in `applications/` and content in `archive/` as references

   Styling rules (do not use `archive/legacy/resume.css` or `cover_letter.css` for new applications):
   - Derive visual design from the JD each time: industry, company stage, role type, team language, and culture cues
   - Embed all CSS inline in a `<style>` block within each HTML file
   - Briefly document styling choices in `meta.json` styling_notes

   After writing HTML files, render PDFs and DOCX with:
   `./scripts/render_application.sh {company_slug}`

   That script also generates `reply_email.txt` (bullets for recruiter replies). Creating Gmail drafts is handled by the GCloud email parser agent — not this agent.

   Update `meta.json` `updated` field when status changes.
